A||N||4||chris6878||87 4cyl stalls...  need help..||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||03-07-2001||03:09 PM||||I have an 87 fiero 2.5 4 cyl.    It starts perfect and runs perfect, until you run it for about 20-30 min. Then when you slow down it wants to stall completely just like turning off the key. Starts right back up, but as soon as you put it in gear (automatic) it jerks real hard and quits. Usually does this quite a few times, or if ya let it sit a few minutes it will go back to normal...       wonder what could cause this?<P>thanks in advance,<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||03-07-2001||03:23 PM||||Sounds like a torque convertor clutch (TCC) problem.  Usually the TCC solenoid in the trans has gone bad.  Do a search and you'll find some good instructions for troubleshooting.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||4
Z||000002||DaveL||03-07-2001||03:52 PM||||Is it an automatic or manual? I would suspect possible ignition problems if it happens after it gets good and warmed up, like maybe an ignition module and\or coil pack. Hope not, because they ain't cheap... You didn't say if any error codes are displayed, or if the check engine light ever goes on.||||reg||3
Z||000003||TheFiero64||03-07-2001||05:23 PM||||It is definitely your TCC clutch. There is a connector at the firewall side of the trans. It has 4 wires in it. Disconnect that and it should run ok until you fix the tcc.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||03-07-2001||09:13 PM||||thanks guys,   i think it would be the TCC too..   sometimes i gets stiff when it wants to shift like from 2 to 3 and it jerks or pops when it doesn go into it, like something is keeping it from it...    <P>thanks for the replies,<BR>chris||||reg||3
